\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 HokieBike Beta Tester Quick Guide
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Purpose
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 This guide explains how to authenticate in the HokieBike app using email link sign-in and how to use the TestFlight invite link.\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Part 1: Installing HokieBike from TestFlight
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 1. Open the TestFlight invite link you received from the HokieBike team.\u8232 2. Tap 
\f0\b Start Testing
\f1\b0 .\uc0\u8232 3. If prompted, install the 
\f0\b TestFlight
\f1\b0 app from the App Store first.\uc0\u8232 4. In TestFlight, tap 
\f0\b Install
\f1\b0 next to HokieBike.\uc0\u8232 5. After install completes, tap 
\f0\b Open
\f1\b0 .\uc0\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Part 2: Logging In with Email Link
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 1. Launch HokieBike.\u8232 2. Enter your email address on the login screen (for pilot testing, use your approved tester email).\u8232 3. Tap 
\f0\b Continue 
\f1\b0 to request a sign-in email link.\uc0\u8232 4. Open your email inbox and look for the HokieBike/Firebase sign-in message.\u8232 5. Tap the sign-in link in that email.\u8232 6. Return to HokieBike (it may open automatically depending on your device setup).\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Important Notes
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 - 
\f0\b Check your Junk/Spam folder
\f1\b0 if you do not immediately see the sign-in email.\uc0\u8232 - Email delivery can take 
\f0\b up to 5 minutes
\f1\b0 in some cases.\uc0\u8232 - If the link fails or expires, go back to HokieBike and request a new link.\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b If the Link Opens in Browser Instead of App
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 1. Copy the full sign-in URL from the browser/email.\u8232 2. Return to HokieBike login.\u8232 3. Paste the URL into the manual sign-in link field (if shown).\u8232 4. Tap 
\f0\b Complete Sign-In from Link
\f1\b0 .\uc0\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Part 3: How the TestFlight Invite Link Works
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 - The invite link grants access to the current approved beta build in TestFlight.\u8232 - Testers install and update HokieBike through TestFlight (not the App Store listing).\u8232 - When a newer build is released, TestFlight shows an 
\f0\b Update
\f1\b0 button.\uc0\u8232 - The invite link itself does not log you into HokieBike; app login is a separate email-link authentication step.\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Quick Troubleshooting
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 - No email received: wait 5 minutes, check Junk folder, then request a new link.\u8232 - Link says invalid/expired: request a fresh email link and use the newest one only.\u8232 - App not visible in TestFlight: confirm you accepted the invite using the same Apple ID used in TestFlight.\u8232 \u8232 
\f0\b Contact
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 If you still cannot sign in, share a screenshot of the error message with the HokieBike team and include the time you attempted login.\u8232 }